$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^4-4x^3+4x^2}{x-2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x^2(x-2)(x-2)}{(x-2)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{{x^2}\cancel{(x-2)}(x-2)}{{}\cancel{(x-2)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x^3-2x^2, \text{ for }x\neq 2
\end{align}$
